Cell["\<\
Rows refer to finalPoints and columns refer to initialPoints. hopping[rf, ri] \
must return a consistently sized matrix for the internal degrees of freedom.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->585226044,ExpressionUUID->"d9acc6dc-7044-fe4e-841f-24b6fe8b4384"],

Cell["\<\
The distance argument must have head Real, for example 1.01 rather than the \
exact integer 1. Only pairs within this Euclidean cutoff are evaluated.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1801281102,ExpressionUUID->"9a5fc188-647b-dd4f-85b9-229b3c1b6dcf"],

Cell["\<\
Point sets may contain coordinate lists or rules label -> coordinates; labels \
are passed to the hopping function when present. Point sets must be nonempty.\
\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->866197622,ExpressionUUID->"afa91a23-2d0d-8a4a-8347-ebb92eeba674"]
}, Closed]],

